        "procedure": "Compounds 1–4 were prepared by the same procedure; only 4 is described in detail and 1 was obtained analogously using Eu(NO3)3·6H2O in place of Dy(NO3)3·6H2O. 2-Hydroxy-3-methoxybenzaldehyde (152 mg, 1.00 mmol) and 2-aminoethanol (76 mg, 1.25 mmol) in MeCN (30 mL) were stirred and heated at 80 °C for 1 h (dark yellow solution). After cooling, triethylamine (405 mg, 4.00 mmol), Ln(NO3)3·6H2O (1.00 mmol) and pivalic acid (102 mg, 1.00 mmol) were added. After stirring 1 h, Co(NO3)2·6H2O (125 mg, 0.50 mmol) and 3-butylene glycol (270 mg, 3.00 mmol) were added (dark red). The mixture was stirred under ambient conditions for 2 h, filtered, and crystals formed after one week, washed with cold MeCN (2 × 5 mL) and dried under vacuum.",
